"""English presentation data; computed charts retain their original Chinese evidence."""
DATA='''The Creative|Strength · Creation|Progress calls for responsibility; excessive force creates imbalance.|A golden dragon rises through an open sky.
The Receptive|Support · Responsiveness|Receive and carry things through; responsiveness does not mean abandoning judgment.|Broad fields support living things.
Difficulty at the Beginning|Beginnings · Order|Early obstacles call for structure before expansion.|A shoot emerges between rocks in a thunderstorm.
Youthful Learning|Learning · Inquiry|Seek reliable guidance while the situation is unclear.|A young traveller seeks a path with a lantern below a mountain.
Waiting|Patience · Preparation|Ability is present, but conditions need preparation and time.|A traveller waits by a river beneath gathering rain clouds.
Conflict|Disagreement · Boundaries|Clarify differences and limits; avoid pursuing victory at any cost.|Two scholars face one another from opposite banks.
The Army|Discipline · Organisation|Success depends on organisation and rules, not individual bravado.|An orderly procession crosses the plain beneath banners.
Holding Together|Alliance · Trust|Choose reliable companions; cooperation needs sincerity and boundaries.|People gather beside the water.
Small Restraint|Accumulation · Gentle Control|Resources are still limited; consolidate before a major advance.|Wind gathers thin clouds over terraces, without rain.
Treading|Care · Proportion|Respect boundaries when approaching a powerful or sensitive situation.|A traveller walks cautiously beside a tiger.
Peace|Exchange · Harmony|Open communication supports progress; favourable conditions still need care.|A bridge connects two banks beneath an open sky.
Standstill|Separation · Protection|Communication is blocked; protect essential boundaries first.|A cliff interrupts a path below a distant sky.
Fellowship|Shared Purpose · Cooperation|Cooperate around an open common purpose rather than a closed clique.|Companions meet in an open landscape.
Great Possession|Abundance · Stewardship|Abundant resources call for careful distribution and restraint.|A bronze vessel holds a rich harvest in sunlight.
Modesty|Substance · Humility|Keep real ability without displaying it excessively; leave room to adjust.|Low hills rest within an expansive, sheltered plain.
Enthusiasm|Energy · Mobilisation|Use shared momentum, while keeping preparation ahead of excitement.|Villagers make music as spring thunder approaches.
Following|Responsiveness · Choice|Follow a sound direction rather than another person blindly.|Travellers follow a light along the river at dusk.
Repairing Decay|Repair · Renewal|Address the causes of accumulated problems, not just their surface.|Craftspeople repair an old ancestral hall.
Approach|Nearness · Responsibility|As possibilities approach, take responsibility; favourable conditions may recede.|An elder visits and attends to people beside a marsh.
Contemplation|Observation · Perspective|Observe the whole situation and your place in it before deciding.|A figure surveys fields from a high terrace.
Biting Through|Obstacles · Clear Judgment|Deal with a real obstruction; judgment and execution both matter.|A bronze blade cuts a knot beneath lightning.
Grace|Appearance · Substance|Presentation can refine substance, but cannot replace it.|A refined pavilion glows below a mountain.
Stripping Away|Erosion · Foundations|As support weakens, protect the foundation rather than force an advance.|An elder reinforces the foot of a house with peeling walls.
Return|Renewal · Rhythm|A small turning point needs a sustainable rhythm to develop.|A shoot emerges as winter ends and a path home appears.
Without Falsehood|Reality · Natural Action|Act on facts; avoid wishful thinking and unnecessary demands.|A white crane stands in open country under a clear thunderous sky.
Great Restraint|Preparation · Cultivation|Build and govern your abilities before putting them into action.|A strong horse rests inside a mountain gate beside study scrolls.
Nourishment|Input · Moderation|Examine what sustains you; speech and resources both need moderation.|Hands offer a bowl of grain below a mountain.
Great Exceeding|Load · Imbalance|Reduce pressure or strengthen the structure when its load is excessive.|A beam bends under a heavy load over a lake.
Repeated Water|Risk · Steady Practice|Repeated risks call for controlled steps, not reckless escape.|Water rushes through successive deep gorges.
Radiance|Clarity · Dependence|Clarity depends on a suitable foundation; examine what supports it.|Two lamps illuminate books and a painted scroll.
Influence|Response · Attraction|Mutual response is possible, but is not a lasting commitment.|Two cranes draw near beside a mountain reflected in a lake.
Duration|Consistency · Adaptation|Lasting progress needs a sustainable rhythm, not rigid repetition.|An old pine holds its ground in wind and thunder.
Retreat|Distance · Preservation|Withdraw at the right time to preserve room for future action.|A traveller takes a distant mountain path.
Great Strength|Power · Boundaries|Growing strength still needs boundaries; avoid forcing your way through.|A ram pauses at a fence beneath thunder.
Progress|Visibility · Advancement|Conditions favour being seen; proceed steadily.|Sunrise lights steps leading to a pavilion.
Darkening of the Light|Discretion · Protection|Protect what matters when open expression is unsafe or ineffective.|A traveller shelters a lamp in a dark valley.
The Family|Roles · Internal Order|Clarify responsibilities and rules within relationships or organisations.|A household shares a warm courtyard and its daily tasks.
Opposition|Difference · Limited Agreement|Seek workable small agreements without pretending differences have vanished.|Two people look toward different horizons.
Obstruction|Difficulty · Assistance|Change the route or seek help rather than force a blocked path.|A traveller faces floodwater in a mountain pass.
Release|Relief · Resolution|As an obstacle loosens, resolve what remains promptly.|A loosened rope appears beneath clearing clouds.
Decrease|Reduction · Trade-offs|Remove unnecessary burdens while recognising the cost of each choice.|A traveller sets down surplus vessels beside a lake.
Increase|Benefit · Action|Direct resources where they can support useful action.|Fresh water nourishes young trees and fields.
Breakthrough|Decision · Openness|Make the decision clear; guard against haste and isolation.|Water passes through an opened embankment.
Encounter|Meeting · Discernment|Examine an unexpected influence before accepting it.|Travellers meet unexpectedly under a windswept tree.
Gathering|Concentration · Shared Centre|Gathering people and resources needs a common centre and order.|Boats converge at a waterside temple.
Pushing Upward|Growth · Gradual Effort|Rise through support and accumulated effort, not one sudden leap.|A young tree grows beside ascending stone steps.
Oppression|Limits · Endurance|When resources are scarce, preserve your capacity for basic action.|A traveller rests beside a dry well and sparse reeds.
The Well|Source · Sustainable Support|Attend to the resource system; a good well must also be accessible.|People draw clean water from an old village well.
Revolution|Change · Readiness|Lasting change needs mature conditions and trust, not a new appearance alone.|An old robe is exchanged for a new one in autumn light.
The Vessel|Transformation · Structure|Resources gain value through organisation and a reliable supporting structure.|A bronze vessel stands above a steady cooking fire.
Thunder|Shock · Composure|Steady yourself before responding to a sudden change.|Thunder shakes trees as a traveller regains composure.
Keeping Still|Pause · Boundaries|Stop where stopping is appropriate.|A person sits quietly between two mountains.
Gradual Development|Stages · Order|Progress requires stages that cannot simply be skipped.|Geese move gradually from the shore toward higher ground.
The Marrying Maiden|Position · Unequal Arrangements|Recognise unequal roles and protect your ability to choose.|A wedding carriage waits near a side entrance.
Abundance|Fullness · Turning Point|Address key matters during a peak while recognising that peaks do not last.|Lanterns and grain stores stand beneath a darkened midday sun.
The Traveller|Temporary Place · Adaptation|As a guest, respect limits, preserve an exit and choose companions carefully.|A lightly equipped traveller arrives at a mountain inn.
The Gentle Wind|Penetration · Persistence|Advance through sustained influence and clear communication.|Wind moves through bamboo and an open window.
The Joyous Lake|Exchange · Integrity|Conversation can build connection; avoid sacrificing principles to please others.|Friends share tea beside connected lakes.
Dispersion|Clearing · Reconnection|After dispersing a blockage, rebuild connections and a shared centre.|Wind clears river mist as boats set out again.
Limitation|Measure · Sustainable Limits|Appropriate limits support continuity; excessive restrictions obstruct it.|A measured channel distributes water among bamboo.
Inner Truth|Sincerity · Consistency|Trust needs inner and outer consistency, supported by observable action.|Two cranes and their clear reflections stand by a calm lake.
Small Exceeding|Small Steps · Care|Make modest corrections rather than enlarge the goal recklessly.|A small bird flies low below mountain clouds.
After Completion|Completion · Maintenance|Once a stage is complete, maintain it and anticipate disorder.|A boat has reached shore while a pot sits over a controlled fire.
Before Completion|Unfinished · Continued Care|One important step remains; do not treat the outcome as settled.|A fox with a wet tail remains beside a river, with the far bank still ahead.'''
IMAGES='The movement of heaven|The yielding earth|Cloud and thunder|A spring below a mountain|Clouds above heaven|Heaven and water move apart|Water within the earth|Water upon the earth|Wind moves above heaven|Heaven above, lake below|Heaven and earth communicate|Heaven and earth do not communicate|Heaven with fire|Fire above heaven|A mountain within the earth|Thunder rises from the earth|Thunder within a lake|Wind below a mountain|Earth above a lake|Wind moves over the earth|Thunder and lightning|Fire below a mountain|A mountain rests upon the earth|Thunder within the earth|Thunder moves beneath heaven|Heaven within a mountain|Thunder below a mountain|The lake overwhelms the trees|Water arrives repeatedly|Brightness arises twice|A lake upon a mountain|Thunder and wind|A mountain beneath heaven|Thunder above heaven|Brightness emerges above the earth|Brightness enters the earth|Wind comes from fire|Fire above, lake below|Water upon a mountain|Thunder and rain arise|A lake below a mountain|Wind and thunder|A lake above heaven|Wind beneath heaven|A lake upon the earth|Wood grows within the earth|A lake without water|Water above wood|Fire within a lake|Fire above wood|Repeated thunder|Joined mountains|Wood upon a mountain|Thunder above a lake|Thunder and lightning arrive together|Fire upon a mountain|Following winds|Joined lakes|Wind moves over water|Water above a lake|Wind above a lake|Thunder upon a mountain|Water above fire|Fire above water'.split('|')
NOTES={15:'The mountain within the earth suggests substantial ability held modestly, rather than weakness.',17:'The dusk journey is a modern metaphor for responding to timing. Following means discerning what deserves to be followed, not blind obedience.',19:'The lakeside visit suggests responsibility and care. It does not make authority infallible or guarantee an opportunity will last.',23:'Peeling walls and strengthened foundations suggest protecting essentials as support weakens, not an inevitable disaster.',24:'The shoot suggests a beginning of renewal, not a guarantee that a particular person will return.',26:'The horse and scrolls express cultivated strength and learning. The term xu here means to accumulate or nurture.',30:'Two lamps suggest sustained clarity and its supporting conditions, not guaranteed wealth or celebration.',43:'The open waterway symbolises a clear decision and removal of an obstruction, not violent destruction.',54:'The carriage represents an unequal arrangement; it does not predict marital failure or judge women.',63:'Reaching shore represents a completed stage that still requires care, not permanent success.',64:'The unfinished crossing suggests a remaining step, not inevitable failure.'}
def attach(hexagrams):
 rows=DATA.splitlines();assert len(rows)==len(IMAGES)==64
 for h,row,image in zip(hexagrams,rows,IMAGES):
  name,theme,meaning,motif=row.split('|');h.update(name_en=name,theme_en=theme,meaning_en=meaning,motif_en=motif,classical_image_en=image,art_note_en=NOTES.get(h['number'],'People and scenery are modern narrative metaphors for the hexagram. Each painted object is not a literal correspondence in the classical text.'))
